From a418623a0963f66228bf78948c949cdd2a4769f7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: alwaysafoujdar <akfaujdar646@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 19:34:04 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Let players join from any network, not just the host's WiFi
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Campus networks isolate clients from one another, so the LAN join URL is
unreachable for half the room even when everyone has full bars.

Nothing in the game needed a LAN — the client already connects to whatever
origin served it. The one exception was /api/network, which built the join URL
and QR code from os.networkInterfaces() and so kept advertising 192.168.x.x
however the server was actually reached.

The join URL is now resolved in order: PUBLIC_URL if set, then the first hop of
X-Forwarded-Proto/Host when the request came through a tunnel or platform
proxy, and otherwise the host's IPv4 as before. The LAN address list is
suppressed when remote, since those addresses would only mislead. Existing
same-WiFi behaviour is unchanged.

README documents both routes: a Cloudflare quick tunnel from the host laptop,
and deploying to a free Node host, with the single-instance and restart caveats
that in-memory state implies.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
